{%- comment -%}
  Does this filter have at least one value that will actually be rendered?

  Accepts: filter (required). Outputs `1` for yes, nothing for no.

  The Color facet is fed from tags, and the tag namespace carries non-colours. lena-color-facet
  drops those from the checkbox list, which is right - but the <fieldset>, <summary> and <ul>
  around the list were rendered before anything checked whether a single <li> would survive.
  If every value were skipped the visitor got a Color accordion that opened onto nothing.

  This asks the question the fieldset should have asked first. It calls the same snippet the
  list itself calls, so the two can never disagree about which values count - asking it any
  other way would be the duplication that lena-color-facet exists to prevent.

  Cost: one extra pass over filter.values per filter, only for boolean and list filters.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign fv_found = false
  for fv_value in filter.values
    capture fv_label
      render 'lena-color-facet', filter: filter, value: fv_value
    endcapture
    assign fv_label = fv_label | strip
    if fv_label != blank
      assign fv_found = true
      break
    endif
  endfor
  if fv_found
    echo 1
  endif
-%}
